+- **Rolling the start place back** (until c0188 deletes the lobby): a tracked fix whose pull request changes that one line back, `"build": "portal"` to `"build": "lobby"` on the Portal place. Its deploy, once it is ready for review, publishes pickman's lobby to the start place, told `GamePlaceId`, as before f0209; Pickman's game keeps `LobbyPlaceId`, so its game over returns to the lobby. Nothing stored moves: plays, free games and passes are in the same records both places read.
 - If any of the three is missing the job skips with a warning instead of failing. Forks never get the secret, and the secret is only in the environment of the steps that need it.
 - Publishes happen one at a time (`beta-deploy`, and a running publish is not cancelled). The comment names the pull request's commit.
 - The job has a 20-minute timeout, because it holds the shared `beta-deploy` lock.
 - The job installs only the tools (`z-nile/setup.sh --tools`).
 - By hand: export the three settings (and each place's variable) and run `lune run scripts/deploy-beta` in `portal/` (the job runs its steps there too). That publishes to Beta.
